{
  "about": [
    "The Tasks card above a session's composer — Tasks created here, merged with what its watches",
    "wait on: its fixed words and the sentence its",
    "collapsed form writes — one set of cases both clients are proved against. The shared",
    "`sessionCreatedTasks.spec.ts` checks `createdTasksCountLine` and `SESSION_CREATED_TASKS_COPY`",
    "(@orbit/shared, what the web renders) against this file; the native client reads the same file,",
    "so the two ends cannot drift into two sentences.",
    "",
    "`copy`: the row's fixed words. `replacesPrefix` is followed directly by the replaced task's",
    "title, `createdInChip` (the Tasks page's filter chip) by the session's title.",
    "",
    "`countLine`: `{running, failed, done, total}` → `text`, the counts exactly as",
    "`GET /sessions/:id/created-tasks` returns them (they count rows, not tasks). `N running` and",
    "`N failed` are written only when N > 0; `done/total done` always is; the parts are joined by",
    "\" · \" (U+00B7 between two spaces).",
    "",
    "`singleNamesTheTask`: when `total` is 1 the collapsed row writes no count sentence; it names",
    "the task and shows its status pill instead, as the Watching row does. With `total` 0 the session",
    "created nothing and there is no row.",
    "",
    "`card`: `sessionTaskCard(created, watched)` — the created answer (`null` when there is none) and",
    "the tasks the session's live watches wait on — to the card it draws, or `null` for no card. `rows`",
    "is the order, each with its eye (`watched`), the eye's orange (`stale`) and whether it was created",
    "elsewhere (no age; `copy.elsewhere` in its place). A watched id marks a created row by the row's",
    "task or the task it replaces, in either spelling (UUID or base62). Watched rows come first; the",
    "sentence counts the created tallies plus the watched tasks created elsewhere."
  ],
  "copy": {
    "title": "Tasks",
    "viewAll": "View all in Tasks ›",
    "openProject": "Open project ›",
    "replacesPrefix": "Replaces ",
    "createdInChip": "Created in ",
    "elsewhere": "elsewhere"
  },
